From aa5421175f4f23046d780294bc1c35558d0a94f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iuri Jikidze <37273763+ijiki16@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:38:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/35] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: reserve the BL31 secure
 monitor

The vendor boot0/boot_package loads BL31 at 0x48000000 and the vendor
DT reserves 16 MiB there (sun60iw2p1.dtsi). The mainline dtsi has no
reserved-memory node, so Linux treats that range as normal RAM. The
kernel can then allocate over the running secure monitor.

The same gap broke booting with an initrd. U-Boot moved a 34 MB
initrd to 0x47e10000..0x49fff46b, over BL31, and the board hung
after "Starting kernel".

Reserve the range as no-map.

Tested on an OrangePi 4 Pro: dmesg shows "reserved mem:
0x48000000..0x48ffffff (16384 KiB) nomap non-reusable bl31@48000000",
and the board boots Armbian (trixie) with an initrd.

Made with the help of an AI coding assistant (Claude).

Fixes: 0f334f298667 ("ARM: dts: sunxi: Add Allwinner A733 device tree")
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 6c7c3fe78..c0469535e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -15,6 +15,18 @@ / {
 	#address-cells = <2>;
 	#size-cells = <2>;
 
+	reserved-memory {
+		#address-cells = <2>;
+		#size-cells = <2>;
+		ranges;
+
+		/* Secure monitor (BL31), loaded here by the vendor boot0/boot_package. */
+		bl31@48000000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x48000000 0x0 0x01000000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+	};
+
 	cpus {
 		#address-cells = <1>;
 		#size-cells = <0>;
